cowbuttons(1) "@VERSION@" "cowbuttons - button panel for cow"

# NAME

cowbuttons - FvwmButtons-style button panel for the cow window manager

# SYNOPSIS

*cowbuttons* [*-c* _path_] [*-h*]

# DESCRIPTION

*cowbuttons* displays a small configurable grid of cells.  Cells can run
*cow*(1) commands, show selected state from cow's status socket, or act as
empty spacers.

Wayland does not provide X11-style arbitrary window reparenting, so
*cowbuttons* does not swallow clients.  Use command buttons to launch or focus
applications, and use cow rules to style or place companion windows.

# OPTIONS

*-c* _path_
	Load _path_ instead of the default configuration file.

*-h*
	Show usage.

# CONFIGURATION

The default configuration file is:

	_$XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME/cow/cowbuttons.conf_

or, when *XDG_CONFIG_HOME* is unset:

	_~/.config/cow/cowbuttons.conf_

The format is line-oriented.  Blank lines and lines starting with *#* are
ignored.  Labels and commands containing whitespace must be quoted.

*cell_width* _N_
	Set the cell width in pixels.  The default is 96.

*cell_height* _N_
	Set the cell height in pixels.  The default is 32.

*rows* _N_
	Set the grid row count.  The default is 1.

*cols* _N_
	Set the grid column count.  When omitted, the largest configured column is
	used.

*font* _name_
	Set the cairo toy-font face used for labels.

*button* _row_ _col_ _label_ _command_
	Create a clickable button.  _command_ is sent to cow through the command
	socket.

*status* _row_ _col_ _type_
	Create a live status cell.  Supported types are:
	*focused-title*, *focused-app*, *current-output*, *current-desk*, and
	*desk-list*.

*spacer* _row_ _col_
	Create an empty cell.

# EXAMPLES

```
cell_width 120
cell_height 32
rows 2
cols 4

button 0 0 "xterm" "exec xterm"
button 0 1 "next" "focus -n"
button 0 2 "prev" "focus -p"
button 0 3 "pager" "exec cowpager"

status 1 0 focused-title
status 1 1 focused-app
status 1 2 current-output
status 1 3 current-desk
```

Remove cowbuttons' own window chrome using a cow rule:

```
decor -d cowbuttons-chrome border.width 0
decor -d cowbuttons-chrome border.handles false
decor -d cowbuttons-chrome titlebar.enabled false
rule -g -Ton-map -ncowbuttons-chrome -s %cowbuttons decor -a cowbuttons-chrome
```

# FILES

_$XDG\_CONFIG\_HOME/cow/cowbuttons.conf_

_~/.config/cow/cowbuttons.conf_

# SEE ALSO

*cow*(1), *moocow*(1), *cowbar*(1), *cowiconman*(1), *cowpager*(1)

